<http://digistrucmed.org/OutcomeEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Outcome Entity" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/page/3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_p0015> <http://digistrucmed.org/pageId> "3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_p0015" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_3756890c1e5fc6e4f303d0d69c5e6674192365d99b5559676ac7dc7c72e24ed8_n0018/tu_0005> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "It is recommended that patients taking amiodarone therapy and digoxin or warfarin generally have their maintenance doses of many commonly used agents, such as digoxin, warfarin, and statins, reduced when amiodarone is initiated and then carefully monitored for the possibility of adverse drug interactions. Adjustment in doses of these drugs and laboratory assessment of drug activity or serum concentration after initiation of amiodarone is recommended. (Strength of Evidence = A)" .
